***
*** Maven path:
***
Maven home: /usr/local/apache-maven-3.9.1/apache-maven-3.9.11

***
*** Create a link to mvn binary and place it in /usr/local/bin:
***
lrwxrwxrwx 1 root root 49 dic 31 10:23 /usr/local/bin/mvn -> ../apache-maven-3.9.1/apache-maven-3.9.11/bin/mvn

***
*** Execute the testNG tests
***
"/usr/local/apache-maven-3.9.1/apache-maven-3.9.11/bin/mvn" test -f "/home/luis/Documents/Projects/VSCprojects/java_testng_poc/demo/pom.xml"

***
*** Where to get the packages from. This gives you a version for you to configure pom.xml
***
https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.seleniumhq.selenium/selenium-java

***
*** How to get the dependency of a package.
***
1) Go to a package folder in maven central. For example selenium-java:
https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.seleniumhq.selenium/selenium-java

2) Select 4.37.0
https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/org.seleniumhq.selenium/selenium-java/4.37.0

3) Scroll down and search for the dependency xml code. Should be something like this:
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.seleniumhq.selenium</groupId>
    <artifactId>selenium-java</artifactId>
    <version>4.37.0</version>
</dependency>

4) Copy and paste in the pom.xml, in the dependencies part.